---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Ambiguous = `...and what tip we are leaving, and tell me what each
person pays.`;

const Questions = `- Is the tip worked out on the whole bill, or on each share?
- How many decimal places? Money has two; Lua does not know that
- What if the bill does not divide evenly - who pays the extra cent?
- What is typed in, exactly? "18" or "0.18" or "18%"?
- What happens if someone types a word instead of a number?`;
//#endregion

const pool = [
  { slug: "cc-tip-split", title: "Tip Split", stars: 1, note: "the friendliest one" },
  { slug: "cc-recipe-scaler", title: "Recipe Scaler", stars: 1, note: "one number in, several out" },
  { slug: "cc-screen-time", title: "Screen Time", stars: 2, note: "needs a remainder" },
  { slug: "cc-fuel-range", title: "Fuel Range", stars: 2, note: "a negative answer is a real answer" },
];
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge Set 1</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">Complete any 2 of the 4 below.</h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Set Is For</h2>

          <p>Everything here takes something in, works something out, and says something back. That is <b>sequencing</b> &mdash; the first of the three building blocks every algorithm is made of, and the only one you have so far.</p>

          <p>No decisions and no loops. If you find yourself needing one, you have read more into the brief than it says.</p>

          <p><b>Write your requirements list before you write any code</b>, and submit both.</p>

        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="requirements">
          <h2>This Set Is About What Nobody Told You</h2>

          <p>
            Every brief below is a person describing what they want, and every
            one of them leaves something out. <b>Finding the gaps is the
            work.</b>
          </p>

          <p>
            Take a fragment of one of them and notice how much it does not say:
          </p>

          <Code
            code={Ambiguous}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="From the Tip Split brief"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            That is a normal way for a person to describe what they want, and it
            is not enough to write a program from. Here is what should end up in
            your requirements list:
          </p>

          <Code
            code={Questions}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Requirements — the questions half"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>There is no right answer to any of those.</b> There is only a
            decision you made or a decision you did not notice. Two programs
            that answer them differently are both correct;{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">a program whose author never thought about
            it is the one that goes wrong in front of somebody.</b>
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="challenges">
          <h2>The Challenges</h2>

          <p>Pick <b>any two</b>.</p>

          <ul class="list-unstyled mt-4">
            {
              pool.map((c) => (
                <li class="mb-2">
                  <i class="si-terminal text-sn-theme me-2"></i>
                  <a href={`/courses/ap-csp-lua/unit-1/${c.slug}`}>{c.title}</a>
                  <span class="ms-2">
                    {Array.from({ length: c.stars }).map(() => (
                      <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
                    ))}
                  </span>
                  <span class="text-body-secondary ms-2">&mdash; {c.note}</span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            For each of the two: <b>the requirements list</b> and{" "}
            <b>the program folder</b>.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">The requirements list is the deliverable
            that is actually being read.</b> The code is evidence you tried to
            satisfy your own list.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>10 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
